   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Using Excel, type =B2 into cell C2 and =0.6*B2+0.4*C2 into cell C3. Then drag cell C3 down to the end of the data to compute the EMA. Drag one more cell down to compute the forecast for 2024. Values are rounded to 4 decimal places using the <code class=\"python\" lang=\"python\">ROUND()</code> function.<br>\n<table>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><b>Year</b></td>\n<td align=\"left\"><b>Deviation</b></td>\n<td align=\"left\"><b>EMA</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">1961</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.003</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.003</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">1962</td>\n<td align=\"right\">−0.027</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.003</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">1963</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.425</td>\n<td align=\"right\">−0.015</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">1964</td>\n<td align=\"right\">−­0.281</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.249</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">1965</td>\n<td align=\"right\">−0.36</td>\n<td align=\"right\">−0.069</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">…</td>\n<td align=\"right\">…</td>\n<td align=\"right\">…</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">2022</td>\n<td align=\"right\">1.223</td>\n<td align=\"right\">1.1981</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">2023</td>\n<td align=\"right\">1.212</td>\n<td align=\"right\">1.2131</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">N/A</td>\n<td align=\"right\">N/A</td>\n<td align=\"right\">1.2124</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\nUsing Python:<br> \n<pre class=\"python\" lang=\"python\"># Import libraries\nimport pandas as pd ## for dataset management\n\n# Read the CSV file into a Pandas DataFrame\ndf = pd.read_csv('USATemps1961-2023.csv')\n\n# Use built-in function ewm() to compute the EMA\nalpha = 0.6\ndf['ema']=df['Deviation'].ewm(span=2/alpha - 1, adjust=False).mean()\n\n# Display the last value of EMA column\nprint(df['ema'].tail(1))\n</pre>\nThe resulting output will look like this:\n<pre class=\"python\" lang=\"python\">62  1.212423\nName: ema, dtype: float64\n</pre>\nThe last item in the “ema” column is the forecasted value: 1.2124."
    },
